I made all three changes from the task and committed them as e3f75b3c (not pushed yet). Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings, fmt check, tests/harness_logic.sh and the module-size gate all pass.

| Command | Exit before | Exit after |
|---|---|---|
| bare yoyo run | 0 | 2 |
| yoyo tree zzz | 1 | 2 |
| yoyo undo zzz | 1 | 2 |
| yoyo grep <no match> | 0 | 1 |
| yoyo find <no match> | 0 | 0 (unchanged) |

The printed text is the same as before. The new integration tests compare the whole of stdout, so a wording change would fail them.

• Why grep exits 1 on no match: I checked what the familiar tools do. grep and git grep both exit 1 when nothing matches, and find exits 0; I ran all three. rg isn't installed on this runner, so its exit 1 comes from its documentation, not a run. A search that can't run (for example a missing directory) still exits 2, and a search with matches still exits 0.
• Bare `run`: this is mapped to exit 2 in src/dispatch_sub.rs. That command had been left at 0 because an in-process test ran it, and exiting there would kill the test binary. That test now checks the function run calls instead, so it never reaches the exit.
• Tests that still exit 0: yoyo grep with a match, bare yoyo undo, yoyo undo 0, and bare yoyo tree inside a git repo.
• Checking the grep test: I set the no-match exit back to 0 and the grep test failed by name. I then put it back in the same command and confirmed with git diff.

One more defect, now issue #1058. The task called the undo --all / --last-commit failure case unconfirmed, but my first probe reproduced half of it. In a repo with no git author set, yoyo undo --last-commit prints "✗ Revert failed: Author identity unknown" and still exits 0. I filed that as #1058. The --all failure case I didn't reproduce, so it stays unconfirmed. The docs mention #1058 so the known gap isn't hidden.

Closing #982: with that row moved to #1058, nothing on #982 is left, so the commit body says Fixes #982. The title starts "Close #982's…", which GitHub may also read as a closing keyword. The push will close the issue either way, so I posted a comment on #982 listing each remaining row and its result next to the sha. The only user-facing link to #982 was the last sentence of the exit-codes paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md. I rewrote it to describe the behaviour instead, and updated that paragraph for the three changes.

